Looking at the commit message and the code, I can see the bug is in how the index prefix is handled. The issue is that in both `cmd/es-index-cleaner/app/flags.go` and `cmd/es-rollover/app/flags.go`, the code unconditionally adds a "-" suffix to the index prefix:

```go
c.IndexPrefix = v.GetString(indexPrefix)
if c.IndexPrefix != "" {
    c.IndexPrefix += "-"
}
```

This causes problems when the index prefix already ends with "-", resulting in double separators like "jaeger--" instead of "jaeger-".

The fix is to check if the index prefix already ends with the separator before adding it.

Let me create a test file that will fail on the current buggy code and pass after the fix:

